st a *feature* or report a *bug*?**\r\n\r\nbug\r\n\r\n<!-- Please ask questions on StackOverflow or the webpack Gitter (https://gitter.im/webpack/webpack). -->\r\n<!-- Issues which contain questions or support requests will be closed. -->\r\n\r\n**What is the current behavior?**\r\nWhen I dynamically import a component that has an `import` statement (for example `import Test from './Test';`) and in webpack config I use `ModuleConcatenationPlugin`, `__esModule: true` disappears after hot reloading and some libraries like `react-loadable` [rely on this information](https://github.com/thejameskyle/react-loadable/blob/master/src/index.js#L103).\r\n\r\n**If the current behavior is a bug, please provide the steps to reproduce.**\r\n1. Clone https://github.com/Dattaya/react-code-splitting\r\n2. `git checkout webpack-absent-esmodule`\r\n3. Install dependencies\r\n4. `npm start`\r\n5. Open `localhost:8080` and a development console\r\n6. Notice that initially `__esModule` property is present: `{__esModule: true, default: ƒ}`\r\n7. Modify `react-code-splitting/example/App/Fat.js` and look into the console, `__esModule` is no longer present: `{default: ƒ}`\r\n\r\n<!-- A great way to do this is to provide your configuration via a GitHub gist. -->\r\n<!-- Best provide a minimal reproduceable repo -->\r\n<!-- If your issue is caused by a plugin or loader file the issue on the plugin/loader repo -->\r\n\r\n**What is the expected behavior?**\r\n `__esModule` flag does not disappear.\r\n\r\n**Please mention other relevant information such as the browser version, Node.js version, webpack version and Operating System.**\r\n```\r\n>ver\r\nMicrosoft Windows [Version 10.0.15063]\r\n>node -v\r\nv6.9.1\r\n>npm ls webpack\r\n`-- webpack@3.5.4\r\n```","closed_by":{"login":"sokra","id":1365881,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU4ODE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1365881?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra","html_url":"https://github.com/sokra","fol